{
  "esm": "1.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "template_from_param_undeclared",
    "description": "INVALID — the template parameter `S` of `total(v, S)` stands for the `from` of a `faq` `ranges` entry (esm-spec §9.6.1), and the call site binds it to `ghost_cells`, which names no declared index set. Substitution does not check the bound value; the expanded range `{\"from\": \"ghost_cells\"}` is refused exactly as a hand-written one is (tests/invalid/faq/undeclared_from_name.esm), with `undefined_index_set`. SCHEMA-VALID, so the schema-only bindings accept it, as they accept that fixture.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "faq",
      "index-set",
      "invalid",
      "resolver",
      "expression_templates"
    ]
  },
